    <item>
      <title>Artwork &amp; Themes</title>
      <link>https://mate-desktop.org/docs/developer/artwork/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://mate-desktop.org/docs/developer/artwork/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;You can contribute to MATE without writing any code by creating wallpapers and GTK themes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Wallpapers&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;wallpapers&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#wallpapers&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Good wallpapers are calm and unobtrusive — many people look at their desktop for hours at a time. MATE-branded imagery is always welcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Useful open-source tools:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://www.gimp.org/&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;GIMP&lt;/a&gt; — raster image editor (photos, compositing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://inkscape.org/&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Inkscape&lt;/a&gt; — vector image editor (crisp at any resolution)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Submit finished wallpapers to the &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/mate-desktop/mate-backgrounds&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;mate-backgrounds&lt;/a&gt; repository.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;GTK Themes&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;gtk-themes&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#gtk-themes&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;MATE uses the &lt;a href=&#34;https://docs.gtk.org/gtk3/&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;GTK 3&lt;/a&gt; toolkit. When designing a theme, the GNOME Human Interface Guidelines 2.2.1 remain a useful reference for MATE&amp;rsquo;s visual conventions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://mbkma.github.io/gnome-2-hig-book/&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;GNOME HIG 2.2.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Submit new themes or improvements to the &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/mate-desktop/mate-themes&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;mate-themes&lt;/a&gt; repository.&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Translation</title>
      <link>https://mate-desktop.org/docs/developer/translation/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://mate-desktop.org/docs/developer/translation/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;Translating MATE into your language is one of the easiest ways to contribute — no programming knowledge required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MATE uses &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.transifex.com&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Transifex&lt;/a&gt; to manage translations. All application strings, desktop file metadata, and help content are available there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How to get started&lt;span class=&#34;hx:absolute hx:-mt-20&#34; id=&#34;how-to-get-started&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#how-to-get-started&#34; class=&#34;subheading-anchor&#34; aria-label=&#34;Permalink for this section&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a free account at &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.transifex.com/signup/&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;transifex.com/signup&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open the &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.transifex.com/projects/p/MATE/&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;MATE project page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find your language team and click &lt;strong&gt;Join team&lt;/strong&gt;. If your language does not exist yet, you can request it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick a resource to translate and start suggesting strings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translations are pulled into the repositories periodically before each release.&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
